Furthermore, to ensure the model remains objective and does not inadvertently guide users towards specific fields based on current biases, it would be beneficial to implement a feedback loop. This could involve regular surveys and focus groups with users, employers, and educational institutions to validate the effectiveness and impartiality of the guidance provided. By continuously assessing and refining the model based on real-world outcomes and user experiences, the risk of oversaturation in certain fields can be minimized, and the model can be adjusted to better align with actual labor market needs and individual career aspirations.

